Z||000007||jimmybpei||11-11-2001||02:05 PM||||Girls and Guys,<P>Contemporary motorsports is out of Calgary Alberta- Canada. They also have the eibach springs for the fiero. This is the spring that i Runn in all my fieros as well as my Accura They do make a big difference in the handleing of the car, especially if you run bigger wheeles (16 17 18 19 20) Like i do.<P>You will not regret changing out your stock springs.<P>Oh by the way if you cant get a telephone number for Contemporary Motorsport get the number fot TnT Honda they are under the same ownership (i think).<P>Later<BR>Jimmmy B.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fieroX||11-11-2001||03:18 PM||||just cut your springs, I love mine.  My car doesnt bounce all around, it actually rides 90% original.  It handles twice as good as original, it didnt cost anything, and it looks awesome.  Contrary to what everyone says about cutting springs (ie Triad) I think mine worked out great.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
